Fix PKCS#11 module double-initialization in apple-codesign.

A PKCS#11 module can only be initialized once per process. rcodesign on
upstream main initializes the module both while resolving the certificate
source and again for each signing operation; the second C_Initialize fails
with CKR_CRYPTOKI_ALREADY_INITIALIZED, which breaks signing with the Google
Cloud KMS PKCS#11 library (and any other PKCS#11 module).

This is based on the apple-codesign/src portion of the upstream fix:
https://github.com/indygreg/apple-platform-rs/pull/350
(head commit 399e5a8e57ba6c35d1c221be7424f6ba3cfddd6b)

It differs from that pull request in one way: the module is never finalized
or unloaded. The pull request calls C_Finalize once signing is done and
drops the module context, which unloads the library. The Google Cloud KMS
library can still have threads running at that point (it does when it
authenticates with Google credentials), and a thread that runs after the
library is unmapped crashes the process with SIGSEGV. That happened
intermittently at the end of a run, after rcodesign had written its signed
output.

Drop this patch once the pull request lands and the pinned revision in
action.yml is bumped past it. Check first that the upstream version does not
bring that crash back.

